.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Provides a managed thread wrapper with event‑based control mechanisms\&. \fBThreadEx\fP supports starting, stopping, pausing, resuming, joining, and sending custom events to the running thread\&. 

The class uses \fBEventGroup<TFastType>\fP for thread state signaling and \fBLightLock\fP for synchronization\&. Several callback hooks allow custom behavior during setup, execution, pausing, cleanup, and termination\&.

.PP
\fBThreadEx\fP is designed for deterministic thread control without relying on heavy synchronization primitives\&. All state transitions are represented as bit flags inside an \fBEventGroup<Fast_Int>\fP\&.

.PP
Reserved event bits: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
0 — Joinable 
.IP "\(bu" 2
1 — Started 
.IP "\(bu" 2
3 — Pause requested 
.IP "\(bu" 2
4 — Continue requested 
.PP

.PP
Custom events may use bits ≥ 4\&. 
