.SS "bool SystemEx\&.Threading\&.ThreadEx\&.Commit (bool end = \fRtrue\fP)"

.PP
Finalizes the active invoke context without adding a message, provided the commit window has not expired\&. If the commit window is still open and \fIend\fP  is true, the invoke context is terminated\&. 
.br
 If the commit window has elapsed, checkEndContext handles the automatic context termination\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIend\fP Indicates whether the invoke context should be terminated\&. 
.br
 When \fRtrue\fP, the invoke-state bit is cleared, the commit window timer is stopped and reset, and the context mutex is released\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRtrue\fP if the invoke context was still active and the commit operation completed successfully; 
.br
 \fRfalse\fP if the commit window had already expired and the context was automatically terminated\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Definition at line \fB375\fP of file \fBThreadEx\&.cs\fP\&.
.SS "bool SystemEx\&.Threading\&.ThreadEx\&.Commit (\fBThreadInvokeMessage\fP type, Object message, byte prio, bool end = \fRfalse\fP)"

.PP
Commits a message into the active invoke context, provided the commit window has not expired\&. If the commit window is still open, the message is appended to the context queue with the specified priority\&. 
.br
 When \fIend\fP  is true, the invoke context is terminated after the message is committed\&.

.PP
If the commit window has already elapsed, the context is automatically closed by checkEndContext and no message is added\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImessage\fP The message payload consisting of a \fBThreadInvokeMessage\fP identifier and an associated object\&. 
.br
\fIprio\fP The priority value assigned to the message\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP Indicates whether the invoke context should be terminated after committing the message\&. 
.br
 When \fRtrue\fP, the invoke-state bit is cleared, the commit window timer is stopped and reset, and the context mutex is released\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRtrue\fP if the message was successfully committed while the invoke context was still active; 
.br
 \fRfalse\fP if the commit window had already expired and the context was automatically closed\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Definition at line \fB425\fP of file \fBThreadEx\&.cs\fP\&.
.SS "bool SystemEx\&.Threading\&.ThreadEx\&.Invoke (int msOpen = \fR1000\fP)"

.PP
Begins a new invoke context by acquiring the context mutex, enabling the invoke-state bit, and opening a timed commit window\&. The commit window duration is defined by \fImsOpen\fP  and is measured using the thread-local commit stopwatch\&. 
.br
 While the invoke-state bit is set, commit operations may enqueue messages or finalize the context until the commit window expires\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImsOpen\fP The duration of the commit window in milliseconds\&. 
.br
 Commit operations must occur within this time span; otherwise the context is automatically terminated by the running thread\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRtrue\fP if the context mutex was successfully acquired and the invoke context was started; 
.br
 \fRfalse\fP if the mutex could not be locked and the invoke context could not be initiated\&. 
.RE
.PP

